0,Kayan language (Borneo) - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kayan_language_(Borneo),"Kayan (Kajan, Kayan proper) is a dialect cluster spoken by the Kayan people of Borneo. It is a cluster of closely related dialects with limited mutual intelligibility, and is itself part of the Kayan-Murik group of Austronesian languages.","Kayan, Rejang",Austronesian
1,Iban people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iban_people,"The Kayan people, who lived in the upper reaches of the Rejang River, used the term disparagingly to refer to the Iban pioneers, whose restless nature and migration patterns made them unwelcome neighbors.","Kayan, Rejang",Austronesian
